If first-order logic were decidable, provability in~$\Th{Q}$ would be
as well, since $\Th{Q} \Proves !A$ iff $\Proves !T \lif !A$, where
$!T$ is the conjunction of the axioms of~$\Th{Q}$.
\end{proof}

