\begin{prop}
  If $\Gamma \Proves !A$ in natural deduction for intuitionistic
  logic, $\Gamma \Proves !A$ in classical logic. In particular, if
  $!A$ is an intuitionistic theorem, it is also a classical theorem.
\end{prop}

target:
\begin{prop}
  که په شهودي منطق کښې د طبيعي استنتاج له مخې $\Gamma \Proves !A$
  وي، نو په کلاسيک منطق کښې هم $\Gamma \Proves !A$ وي۔ په تېره بيا،
  که $!A$ شهودي قضيه وي، نو کلاسيکه قضيه هم ده۔
\end{prop}

source:
\begin{proof}
  Every natural deduction rule is also a rule in classical natural
  deduction, so every !!{derivation} in intuitionistic logic is also
  !!a{derivation} in classical logic.
\end{proof}

target:
\begin{proof}
