If $A$ can be well-ordered, then $\card{A}$ is the least ordinal
$\gamma$ such that $\cardeq{A}{\gamma}$. For any ordinal $\gamma$, we
say that $\gamma$ is a \emph{cardinal} iff $\gamma = \card{\gamma}$.
\end{defn}

